Farida,

Apologies for the delay on this. I said Friday and it is now Thursday of the
week after. I did not want to answer an estimate with another estimate, so I
waited for a clean run.

Attaching XL-03_scd2_load_impact.xlsx. The measurement, the assumptions behind
it and three scenarios are all in there. Please work from the workbook and not
from this mail. What is below is only the headline.

1. Measured on DEV on 21-Apr. MAP_DIM_CUSTOMER goes from 4 min 12 sec to
11 min 40 sec with SCD2 switched on. The delta is 7 min 28 sec. It is lower
than the figure in your mail of 16-Apr. It is also not zero, and I am not
going to present it as though it were free.

2. I modelled it against the actual nights in the sample rather than against
the average, because your point 4 was the real point and the average was
never the argument. On the worst month end night in that sample the run moves
to finishing 04:20 IST. Against an availability SLA of 05:30 that leaves 70
minutes of head room. On an ordinary night the load still starts at 01:00 and
still closes around 02:05, and the delta disappears into the noise.

3. My conclusion is that the load window cost of SCD2 on DIM_CUSTOMER is
acceptable, and the workbook is me saying so in writing rather than in a
meeting. If your reading of the same numbers is different I would much rather
hear it before the design session than during it.

4. Two caveats, and I would rather flag them myself than have you find them.

   a. The measurement is on DEV, and the DEV copy of ORION was last refreshed
   on 11-Mar-2026, so the volumes are not today's volumes. The assumptions
   sheet (sheet 3, or 4, whichever it ended up as) says exactly what I scaled
   and by how much. If you disagree with the scaling factor, change it in the
   sheet, the rest recalculates.

   b. Everything in the model is elapsed time for the mapping. I have not
   modelled contention with anything else that is running on the host at that
   hour. That needs a night on UAT and I do not have one yet.

On the separate history table. I have not ignored the question, and it is a
fair one. It is a modelling question rather than a load question and I do not
want to answer it in a mail at ten to ten at night, because the answer depends
on what the fact join is allowed to do and on what the reporting layer is
allowed to see. Give me until the design session and I will take it properly
with both options written down side by side, and you can shoot at whichever
one deserves it.

Karthik

